10	assistant	# Concept\n\nA **Venn diagram** is a visual diagram used in mathematics (specifically Set Theory) to show the relationships between different groups or sets of items.\n\nHere are the key components of a Venn diagram:\n\n1. **Universal Set ($\\mathcal{E}$ or $U$):** This represents the entire group being considered. It is drawn as a large outer **rectangle**.\n2. **Sets (Subsets):** These are specific groups within the universal set, represented by **circles** inside the rectangle.\n3. **Intersection ($A \\cap B$):** The overlapping area between two circles. It contains elements that belong to **both** Set $A$ and Set $B$.\n4. **Union ($A \\cup B$):** The total area covered by both circles combined. It contains elements that belong to Set $A$, or Set $B$, or both.\n5. **Complement ($A'$):** The area outside circle $A$. It contains all elements that are **not** in Set $A$.\n\n### The Fundamental Set Formula:\nFor two overlapping sets $A$ and $B$, the sum of elements in all regions equals the total number of elements in the universal set:\n$$n(\\mathcal{E}) = n(A\\text{ only}) + n(B\\text{ only}) + n(A \\cap B) + n(A \\cup B)'$$\n\n---\n\n# Step-by-Step Solution\n\nTo understand how a Venn diagram works, let us solve a standard UNEB-style problem using a Venn diagram.\n\n**Problem:** \nIn an S.1 class of $30$ students at Jinja College, $18$ students play Football ($F$), $15$ play Volleyball ($V$), and $5$ students play neither game. Represent this information on a Venn diagram and find how many students play **both** games.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Define the given information and variables\n* Total number of students, $n(\\mathcal{E}) = 30$\n* Students who play Football, $n(F) = 18$\n* Students who play Volleyball, $n(V) = 15$\n* Students who play neither game, $n(F \\cup V)' = 5$\n* Let the number of students who play both games be $x$, so $n(F \\cap V) = x$\n\n*(Why? We start by letting the unknown overlap region be $x$ so we can write all other regions in terms of $x$.)*\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Express each region of the Venn diagram\n* **Football only:** $18 - x$\n* **Volleyball only:** $15 - x$\n* **Both Football and Volleyball:** $x$\n* **Neither game (outside the circles):** $5$\n\n*(Why? The total number in circle $F$ is $18$. Since $x$ of them are in the overlapping region, those who play Football ONLY must be $18 - x$.)*\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Draw the Venn diagram layout\n\n```text\n+---------------------------------------------------+\n|  Universal Set (\\mathcal{E}) = 30                 |\n|                                                   |\n|     +------------------+   +------------------+   |\n|     | Football (F)     |   | Volleyball (V)   |   |\n|     |                  	2026-09-13 22:58:15.660981+00	5
