1	Summarise	Here is a summary of the provided document excerpts:\n\n### Summary of Course Details: MTH 1101 (Discrete Mathematics)\n\n1. **Course Personnel & Code [Page 1]:**\n   * **Course Code:** Discrete Mathematics ($MTH\\ 1101$)\n   * **Lecturer:** Gershom Buri (bgershom@must.ac.ug)\n   * **Teaching Assistants:** Adelin Habimana, Tracy Natukunda, and Ark Akandinda\n   * **Date:** 8/12/2025\n\n2. **Course Description [Page 2]:**\n   * Introduces fundamental concepts in Discrete Mathematics, with an emphasis on applications in Computer Science and Software Engineering.\n   * Helps students develop a logical mode of thought applicable to both computer hardware and software design.\n\n3. **Why Study Mathematics? [Page 3]:**\n   * Computation obeys strict rules even though it cannot be seen or touched.\n   * Mathematics serves as the universal language needed to reason about these processes.\n   * Major technological inventions are rooted in mathematics (e.g., Bitcoin, Facebook, Google search, and AI).\n   * It is important for LeetCode.\n\n4. **Course Objective [Page 4]:**\n   * To develop logical thinking and reasoning.\n\n*(Note: Page 5 could not be retrieved from the document [Page 5]).*\n\n---\n\n### Common Mistakes Made by Students\n\n1. **Including Outside Information:** Writing facts or definitions about Discrete Mathematics that are not explicitly stated in the given document text.\n2. **Missing Page Citations:** Failing to cite the exact page numbers (e.g., [Page 1], [Page 2]) alongside each summarized point.\n3. **Incorrect Notation Formatting:** Writing mathematical symbols or variables outside of proper dollar-sign LaTeX delimiters ($...$).	2026-09-14 14:05:23.537795+00	6	1	1
